  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "Let \\(P\\) units be the increase in the circumference of a circle resulting from an increase of \\(\\pi\\) units in the diameter. Then \\(P\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac1\\pi\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\pi\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{\\pi^2}{2}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\pi^2\\)",
    "E": "\\(2\\pi\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A circle's circumference is \\(C=\\pi d\\), where \\(d\\) is its diameter. If the original diameter is \\(d>0\\), increasing it by \\(\\pi\\) changes the circumference by\n\\[\nP=\\pi(d+\\pi)-\\pi d=\\boxed{\\pi^2}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
